{"conjecture": "The best technique is refinement types paired with property-based test generation: encode the abstract specification as dependent types that the compiler checks, then auto-extract test oracles from those same types to falsify edge cases the type checker cannot reach. This dual enforcement means the executable code is correct by construction for the cases the types cover and empirically validated for the cases they miss, closing the gap between specification and behavior. The approach fails if the specification language cannot express the relevant invariants or if the type checker's undecidability threshold is too low for the domain."}
